      "responseContract": "appcall-provider-json-v1",
      "adaptations": [
        "Credential-only healthcheck maps to official GET /v1/keys/{key} used by the pinned validator. This is a key-availability read, not a billed address retrieve.",
        "Native also sends the global api_key query parameter used by most AddressZen routes; the pinned keys helper omits that query and puts the key only in the path.",
        "Returns raw AddressZen JSON under data. The upstream user-agent is not sent."
      ]
    },
    "addresses.find": {
      "upstreamActionId": "find_address",
      "sourceRefs": [
        "action-find-address",
        "handler-find-address",
        "build-addresszen-url"
      ],
      "documentationUrls": [
        "https://docs.addresszen.com/docs/api/find-address.md",
        "https://docs.addresszen.com/docs/api/api-reference.md"
      ],
      "responseContract": "appcall-provider-json-v1",
      "adaptations": [
        "Maps to official GET /v1/autocomplete/addresses. Official authentication examples use query name q; pinned source sent query. Native binds input query to wire q. Official 150-character query cap is not expressed as JSON Schema maxLength because strict-generated schemas reject that keyword.",
        "Optional context, country, and limit (1\u2013100) match the pinned action. Official docs: autocomplete does not decrement balance; retrieve does."
      ]
    },
